meta {
  name: 08_PersonLookupFailures
  seq: 8
}

docs {
  Scenario: Failed person lookups are rejected and then throttled

    Given the assistant is not an administrator for the bostyrer
    When the last name does not match the SSN the request fails
    When the person is unknown the request fails
    And the failed lookups are repeated until a pod refuses them
    Then the assistant was not added
    When the bostyrer has failed too many lookups even a valid add is throttled
    And the assistant is revoked as cleanup

    Opt-in. Every step skips itself unless the environment variable runPersonLookupNegatives
    is `true`, for example:

      bru run test/EnduserAPI/BankruptcyEstateAdministrator --env AT22 --env-var runPersonLookupNegatives=true

    Running it locks the bostyrer out of person lookups for an hour
    (FailedAttemptsCacheLifetimeSeconds) on every pod that recorded two failures, so the adds in
    scenarios 01, 02 and 06 fail with 429 on those pods until then. Run it alone, on a quiet
    environment, and not more than once an hour.

    The counter is held in each pod's memory and the client cannot pin requests to one pod
    (observed in AT22: six valid adds right after two failures returned 200 429 429 200 200
    429). Steps 04 and 06 therefore repeat their request until a pod in the expected state
    answers, up to eight times, instead of asserting a single response. That makes the
    scenario independent of routing as long as a pod is reached within those attempts.
}
